# Day 39/50 — Load Balancing

Imagine hundreds of people trying to enter through just one door while several other doors remain unused.

The result? 
A crowded entrance and unnecessary waiting

Web servers can face a similar problem when too many requests reach one server.

**Load Balancing** distributes incoming traffic across multiple servers to prevent any single server from becoming overloaded.
It helps improve performance, availability and reliability.

Instead of making one system handle everything, the workload is shared.

And there's something worth noticing here.

Growth isn't always about making one person or system do more. 
Sometimes, it's about distributing the responsibility better

**Because a system becomes stronger when the load doesn't fall on just one part of it.**
